Every day, I use many cloud services without realizing it. Three cloud services that I often use are Google Drive, Messenger, and Canva. 
These applications help me with my school work, communication, and creating projects.

Google Drive is an example of Software as a Service (SaaS) because I can store, access, and share my files online without installing special software.
It uses the Public Cloud because anyone can create an account and use the service through the internet. 
Messenger is also SaaS because it lets me send messages, make calls, and share files using a web-based application.
It is also a Public Cloud service since it is available to anyone with an account. Canva is another SaaS application because I can design presentations, posters, and other graphics online.
It also uses the Public Cloud because users from anywhere can access it through the internet.

I learned that version control is very important when working on cloud projects. It helps save every change made to files, so nothing is lost.
If someone makes a mistake, it is easy to go back to an older version. Git and GitHub make teamwork easier because many people can work on the same project at the same time.
GitHub keeps track of every change, shows who made the changes, and helps avoid conflicts when editing files. Because of this, teams can work together better, fix problems faster,
and manage cloud projects in a more organized and reliable way.
